Package: brtps
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Regularized Thin Plate Splines for Spatial Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Joaquin", "Cavieres", , "joaquin.cavieres@imng.uni-stuttgart.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Giovanni", "Tasso", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Fits Bayesian spatial regression models in which the spatial
    random field is approximated with the regularized thin plate spline
    ('regTPS') construction of Cavieres and Krumscheid (2026)
    <doi:10.1007/s11222-026-10990-x>. The field is a truncated
    Karhunen-Loeve expansion built from the eigendecomposition of the thin
    plate spline penalty matrix, sampled with a non-centred
    parameterization. Models are written in 'TMB'; posterior inference uses
    the sparse no-U-turn sampler of 'SparseNUTS', with 'tmbstan' and a
    Laplace approximation as alternatives.
